        },
        "question_WkqMGT": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "enso",
            "question": "Can I swap batteries mid-session in ENSŌ?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely — pop in a charged pack and resume immediately.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_NA9RHj": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "enso",
            "question": "How do I turn ENSŌ on and off?",
            "answer": "<p>Press and hold the Thermodial for three seconds. Orange LED indicator pulses = heating. Repeat to power down.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_hV3LRi": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "enso",
            "question": "What temperature range and modes are available?",
            "answer": "<p>Rotate the Thermodial 180–330 °C in 5° steps. Triple-press to activate G-Mode, which skips the 70° pre-heat and delivers a faster, flatter heat curve.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_eBkCXn": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "enso",
            "question": "What do the LED colours indicate?",
            "answer": "<p>• Orange – Standard mode/heating<br/>• Green – G-Mode active<br/>• Blue – Temperature locked<br/>• Red – Low battery</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_EB6eGV": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "enso",
            "question": "What's the difference between ENSŌ Regular Orange mode and Green mode?",
            "answer": "<p>In regular mode, the temperature is regulated by ENSŌ's sophisticated heating algorithm. Features a 70°C+ pre-heat in a 5-minute pre-heating program.<br/>In Green mode, the power distribution is more linear to counterbalance the cooling from more frequent draws. Features no extra heat in the 5-minute pre-heating time.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_QnUEmL": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "enso",
            "question": "How to turn ENSŌ into Green mode?",
            "answer": "<p>To get the device into Green mode you should press the Thermodial 3 times.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_kQqHaP": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "enso",
            "question": "How do I lock or unlock the temperature?",
            "answer": "<p>Press the Thermodial 5 times consecutively to toggle Lock (blue LED).</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_4rhgWT": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "enso",
            "question": "How do I pause a session?",
            "answer": "<p>Turn the Thermodial down to 180 °C. The bowl will stay warm for up to 20 minutes; dial back up to resume.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_mmnJyz": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "enso",
            "question": "Can I adjust the draw or airflow in ENSŌ?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. First, avoid overpacking — keep the load between 8 and 15 g and leave a clear chimney in the centre of the bowl. If the pull is still too restricted, attach the optional Hose Adapter and any wide-bore (≈11–12 mm) silicone hose; the larger diameter can nearly double airflow for an effortless draw.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_XrGnma": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "enso",
            "question": "What materials and dimensions does the ENSŌ have?",
            "answer": "<p>Zinc-alloy body, stainless-steel air path, heat-stable ceramic bowl, crystal-glass tank; footprint 33 × 12 cm.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_zKkwMW": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "enso",
            "question": "What are the battery specifications?",
            "answer": "<p>5,000 mAh / 55 Wh Li-ion, USB-C PD input 5–20 V (max 45 W). Pass-through vaping is supported once the pack has at least 5% charge.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_CWzABb": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "tab": "enso",
            "question": "Is ENSŌ airline-friendly?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Each battery is well below the 100 Wh carry-on limit. Empty the water tank, remove the pack and store batteries in cabin luggage.</p>"
